#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1435e028-99d2-5627-b830-911174be3e37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365378} {:answer/id #uuid "9e993d76-5d6e-5f57-bba0-265da0bc8945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365379} {:answer/id #uuid "49840418-28a8-5eca-8345-fbb5b95e6529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365380} {:answer/id #uuid "42f4146c-1875-5481-aa6e-e32e3c2c16b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365381} {:answer/id #uuid "00d55826-3190-5a37-a80a-04f64ab94c98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42f4146c-1875-5481-aa6e-e32e3c2c16b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365381} :answer-field/id #uuid "27f1bac3-5478-5043-b94f-4b5e882a771d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99d7aeb0-f499-5945-8df6-2ed6bcdeb02c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161707" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{8}z\\,dy]dA\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 4}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}z\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}z[y]_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=8}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(8-{x}^{3})[{\\int }_{0}^{4}z\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(8-{x}^{3}){[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=4}\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{[8x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =8(16-4) \\\\  & =96\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b3b0ebc-7d21-5c71-a721-332d43af1174" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365385} {:answer/id #uuid "7a060360-f156-5748-aff7-a371cead9a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365386} {:answer/id #uuid "a14914d8-167e-54df-abc7-7cd270fbff56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365387} {:answer/id #uuid "a78fa246-c089-53e2-a15c-5dbe923a5fb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365388} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ea7d75-5311-56b3-82e1-01e10e2e95c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a060360-f156-5748-aff7-a371cead9a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365386} :answer-field/id #uuid "71963b0e-cb06-5435-90a3-bd88b0dc18b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62ec7383-3add-5783-838d-5ccce9844f89" :question/math-academy-id "q-161781" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}6y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,x\\le y\\le 1-z},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the $z$-axis,  and the curve $z=1-x$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}6y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{1-z}6y\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{1-z}6y\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}3[{y}^{2}]_{y=x}^{y=1-z}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/819b5b00967bf485068c146602bf962481b21b75d5319113fd6bd94366e84be0.png)\n\n \n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA & ={∬}_{D}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-(1-z)^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1-x}-3{x}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-{x}^{3}+1-3{x}^{2}(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\,\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-{x}^{3}+x]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(\\,\\frac{1}{2}-1+1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ecea781-e9c8-5466-9fdd-87247b399b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365392} {:answer/id #uuid "48018ee4-99b8-5569-8237-2eac9f1f6af5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365393} {:answer/id #uuid "1e172e0f-2815-58d5-876f-c1d82ada6dd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365394} {:answer/id #uuid "23ab1ed5-f014-50fa-95a5-86d98fd53cc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365395} {:answer/id #uuid "43e1218d-1686-5faf-a74d-aa659e7074f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ecea781-e9c8-5466-9fdd-87247b399b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365392} :answer-field/id #uuid "64ab83e3-34fe-58d5-af51-8fbbc1cca887" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86b32cbc-034e-5e5d-a572-7bdac44abc92" :question/math-academy-id "q-161853" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/a1e4a1e39c85a037f3f4f49910b651300363ef34bee969464f5e711aa00986e3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/9165163be9ce95e7165f04d26e6ce8080699ab4d477eba3f804c849fdf1fb679.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/ca74bf149c1371fe9f1622586d9eb92fe180a9c9bb6a0c53d16f538b3c55f4a4.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z[y]_{y=0}^{y=4-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z(4-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[8{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx & ={[12{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(12-0) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ced0079b-bb9d-59e1-acda-9c6a3179d2e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365399} {:answer/id #uuid "577db99d-685d-5971-9333-5ba8fd225b0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365400} {:answer/id #uuid "1e7e04cb-4ca2-568a-bc6e-ca0b1558c1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365401} {:answer/id #uuid "48c9c8fd-b99a-512f-9a57-971387f731a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365402} {:answer/id #uuid "d6fd3211-7e10-5e56-a787-604f79b01d2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "577db99d-685d-5971-9333-5ba8fd225b0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365400} :answer-field/id #uuid "9beacf14-34cf-50c2-82fb-15fe2d583a4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "98d947ff-3e63-571a-956d-fa65049b909f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163717" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/4be9362c014a7b8f0d0708ca5d7ea32a1b5bb13d48e2e1704341d04b89f9566a.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type III region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\,\\text{d}V=$" :question/worked-solution "For a type III region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type III region enclosed between the back surface $y={u}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and the front surface $y={u}_{2}(x,z)=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/63cffdee00edd80c4a0abdc30e8e45b1af29078b8bc4902bf3f60b7b4a104172.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type II *plane* region in the $xz$-plane with the right curve\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/dc72aeb4b554d88f00083dc6bf6f8ca4244e1b7683c8dec10ba0491c678a5603.png)\n\nHence, $D={(x,z)\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡z}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3b9c194-ff23-5544-8f88-b6a6f22df761" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131739} {:answer/id #uuid "c5b1034d-d4d5-53af-bc46-d81b8ab70433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131740} {:answer/id #uuid "e3779082-cfde-5151-a05a-9869224b51d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131741} {:answer/id #uuid "13e80975-720a-5f81-aa95-39708a4c72c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131742} {:answer/id #uuid "473af51c-c038-5d73-9f66-d1aa857dc119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3779082-cfde-5151-a05a-9869224b51d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131741} :answer-field/id #uuid "8446437d-8499-5d66-8517-ad719c5d7b3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da6fd76e-d975-5906-a711-4e6478775eef" :question/math-academy-id "q-40446" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le z\\le 2{x}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 2xz}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2xz}2x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2xz}2x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{2xz}2x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}2x[y]_{y=0}^{y=2xz}dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}2x(2xz)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}4{x}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}4{x}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}4{x}^{2}z\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}[{z}^{2}]_{z={x}^{2}}^{z=2{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}((2{x}^{2})^{2}-({x}^{2})^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{6}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{6}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{6{x}^{7}}{7}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
